<p>
  Contacts (people) and companies (organizations) are shared by every part of Zippiker. A company
  you invoice is the same record your sales team follows up with, so history is never split.
</p>

<h2>Adding people and companies</h2>
<ol>
  <li>
    Open <.link navigate="/contacts">Contacts</.link>
    or <.link navigate="/companies">Companies</.link>.
  </li>
  <li>Click <strong>+ Contact</strong> or <strong>+ Company</strong>.</li>
  <li>Fill in what you know. For a person you can pick their company: start typing its name.</li>
</ol>
<p>
  The person's page shows everything about them: deals, activity timeline, tasks, quotes and invoices.
</p>

<h2>Addresses</h2>
<p>
  On a contact or company page, the <strong>Addresses</strong>
  card holds billing, shipping and office
  addresses. Click <strong>Add →</strong>
  to add one; hover an address to edit or remove it.
</p>

<h2>Finding people fast</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The search box matches names, emails and phone numbers as you type.</li>
  <li>
    If your workspace has dropdown or yes/no <.link navigate="/help/custom-fields">custom fields</.link>,
    filters for them appear next to the search box, e.g. “Tier: Gold”.
  </li>
  <li>
    Tags (comma separated, like <em>vip, newsletter</em>) help you group people your own way.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Owners</h2>
<p>
  Every record can have an <strong>owner</strong>: the teammate responsible for it. Owners default
  to whoever created the record and can be changed any time.
</p>
